  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indian government is preparing for a special session of Parliament scheduled to begin on November 30, with a focus on debating critical legislative reforms. Central to the agenda are the constituency delimitation process and the implementation of the Women’s Reservation Bill, which aims to provide 33% seat quotas for women in legislative bodies. Although the reservation bill was passed in September 2023, it remains in a state of pending enforcement, leading to public criticism from opposition members regarding the delay. The Union Cabinet is currently reviewing proposed amendments to these bills to secure sufficient parliamentary support. This legislative push has triggered intense political maneuvering, with parties like the YSRCP signaling conditional backing while other leaders, such as Akhilesh Yadav and representatives of the Congress, challenge the government's current strategy and historical commitment to these reforms.",
